---
import Tool from '../../layouts/Tool.astro';
const faq = [
  { q: 'How many confirmations do I need?', a: 'One confirmation already makes reversal very unlikely for everyday amounts. Many exchanges and shops wait for 3 to 6 confirmations for larger payments. There is no single “done” number — it depends on how much is at stake.' },
  { q: 'Why does “not found” not mean failed?', a: 'Bitcoin has no failure receipt. An ID that is not on mainnet right now may have a typo, belong to another network, have been replaced by a fee-bump, have been dropped from mempools, or simply not have propagated yet. This tool says so and never claims certainty.' },
  { q: 'Does auto-refresh notify me?', a: 'No. It only updates this page while it is open and visible. Closing the tab, locking your phone or switching away pauses it. There are no push notifications and no backend watching on your behalf.' },
  { q: 'Can I track Lightning payments?', a: 'Not here. Lightning settles off the Bitcoin blockchain. Use the payment request decoder to read a Lightning invoice, and your Lightning wallet to see whether it was paid.' },
  { q: 'Is watching my own address private?', a: 'Looking up an address on mempool.space links that address to your IP for that request. If that matters, use Tor or a VPN, or run your own explorer. Auto-refresh repeats the lookup every 30 seconds while enabled.' },
  { q: 'What if the sender bumped the fee?', a: 'Replace-by-Fee creates a new transaction ID. The old one disappears from mempools and this tracker will show “not found”. Ask the sender for the new ID, or watch the receiving address instead.' },
];
---
<Tool slug="bitcoin-payment-tracker" title="Bitcoin Payment Tracker — watch a txid or address for confirmations" description="Track a Bitcoin payment by transaction ID or address: confirmed with confirmation count, waiting in the mempool with fee context, or not found (with honest uncertainty). Optional 30-second auto-refresh." h1="Payment tracker" lead="Paste a transaction ID or an address to see whether a payment has confirmed. Optional auto-refresh keeps the page up to date while you leave it open — no accounts, no notifications." faq={faq}>
  <Fragment slot="tool">
    <form id="pt-form">
      <label for="pt-input">Transaction ID or Bitcoin address</label>
      <div class="row">
        <input id="pt-input" class="mono" placeholder="txid… or bc1q… / 1… / 3…" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required />
        <div style="flex:0 1 200px"><label for="pt-auto">Auto-refresh</label>
          <select id="pt-auto"><option value="off" selected>Off</option><option value="on">Every 30 seconds</option></select></div>
        <div style="flex:0 1 auto"><button type="submit">Track</button></div>
      </div>
    </form>
    <p class="small muted">Lookups go to mempool.space (mainnet). Auto-refresh only runs while this tab is visible.</p>
    <p id="pt-status" class="small muted" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <div id="pt-result" class="result" aria-live="polite"></div>
  </Fragment>

  <h2>Watching a Bitcoin payment</h2>
  <p>Once you send or expect bitcoin, you usually want a simple answer: has it confirmed? A transaction starts in the <strong>mempool</strong> — the network’s waiting room — and becomes final only when a miner includes it in a block. Each block built on top of that one is another <strong>confirmation</strong>.</p>
  <p>This tracker looks the payment up on the public mempool.space API and explains the result in plain English. For a transaction ID it tells you whether it is confirmed (and with how many confirmations), still waiting (with its fee rate compared to the current market), or not found. For an address it lists recent incoming payments and their status.</p>
  <h3>Why “not found” is careful language</h3>
  <p>Bitcoin does not publish a “failed” receipt. An ID that does not appear may have a typo, may live on testnet, may have been replaced by a higher-fee version (RBF), may have been dropped after sitting too long, or may simply not have reached this explorer yet. The tool lists those possibilities and stops short of guessing.</p>
  <h3>Auto-refresh</h3>
  <p>Turn on the 30-second refresh if you want the page to keep checking while it stays open and visible. It is intentionally polite to the API, pauses when the tab is hidden, and never sends notifications. Close the tab when you are done.</p>
  <h3>Unconfirmed is not final</h3>
  <p>Until a payment has at least one confirmation it can still be replaced, especially under full-RBF. Do not ship goods or mark an order paid on an unconfirmed transaction unless you accept that risk.</p>

  <Fragment slot="example">
    <p>Paste the famous first peer-to-peer payment, <code>f4184fc596403b9d638783cf57adfe4c75c605f6356fbc91338530e9831e9e16</code>. The tracker reports it as confirmed in block 170 with hundreds of thousands of confirmations. Paste a brand-new txid and you will see “waiting in the mempool” with an honest fee-rate comparison. Paste a made-up ID and you get “not found”, with the caveats above — never a claim that it “failed”.</p>
  </Fragment>
</Tool>
<script>import '../../scripts/tracker.ts';</script>
